Session 10 closes at the relay boundary. Summary:

**Three kernel fixes landed (0.11.35 → 0.11.39, build 420FBA28 deployed cluster-wide), each RULE-4 proven live before patching:**

1. **Front B (drc size=0 data loss) — root-caused and fixed.** The reload-identical path re-synced VFS i_size down to the lagging on-disk size mid-append; writeback then discarded the pages as beyond-EOF and the unwritten-conversion size advance clamped to zero (proven with paired P-RELOAD-SIZESEVER/P-WU-CLAMP probes on the exact failing inode). Fix: keep VFS i_size when the reload kept in-core state (`reload_size_keep=1` default). A side discovery: on this 6.19 base, `xfs_setfilesize` is dead code for buffered appends — the size advance lives in `xfs_iomap_write_unwritten`.

2. **Front A (300ms round-open staircase) — fixed.** The ACQUIRING-deferred BAST honor site armed the release dwork for the full 300ms window instead of grace slices; create phases dropped from ~10s to 1.3-2s. The faster handoffs exposed two latent classes, both fixed: a TCP abandoned-mirror-grant convoy (a granted-but-never-consumed grant wedged release 126s while every escape was reset by the starving reader's own ACQUIRING — new `P15-TCP-ORPH-PROCEED` escape keyed on `acq_inflight==0`), and the run_bounded 1s-poll quantization in the test harness.

3. **Cascade amplifier — fixed.** A force-shutdown node's grants stayed in master tables while its dead FS could never serve BASTs, so peers starved to terminal timeouts and shut down too (1 root + 5 dominoes during fio@32). Withdraw now wire-releases everything (`mxfs_dlm_withdraw_release_all`).

**Matrix state: tcp 2/4/8/16/32 all 20/20 green on the one build, every cell within budget** — including first-ever drc@32 greens (102-107s) and all five 32-node budget debts closed via the established N-invariant treatments (fio rand floor, fairness total, crash rotated-subset verify). The fio-vs-xfs yardstick got time-paired median ceilings per rung plus a merge fix in the capture script. 1/tcp has one row pending re-run after the ceiling capture wiped the LUN. Front C's leak probe stayed at zero all session.

**Remaining: 1/tcp final row, the untouched cawp ladder, cawd/caw regression spot-checks (the fixes are transport-shared), then the final one-build enforcing sweep of all four conditions.** Criteria not yet met — the run continues in the next session.

